# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Yaml Front Matter Hash Value: title
#, no-wrap
msgid "Equivalence of the representations"
msgstr "Equivalência das representações"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore vectorizing */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore bilinearity */}\n"
msgstr ""
"{/* cspell:ignore operatorname */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore orthogonalization */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore vectorizing */}\n"
"{/* cspell:ignore bilinearity */}\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've now discussed three different ways to represent channels in mathematical terms, namely Stinespring representations, Kraus representations, and Choi representations.\n"
"We also have the definition of a channel, which states that a channel is a linear mapping that always transforms density matrices into density matrices, even when the channel is applied to just part of a compound system.\n"
"The remainder of the lesson is devoted to a mathematical proof that the three representations are equivalent and precisely capture the definition.\n"
msgstr ""
"Até agora discutimos três formas diferentes de representar canais em termos matemáticos: representações de Stinespring, representações de Kraus e representações de Choi.\n"
"Também temos a definição de canal, que estabelece que um canal é um mapeamento linear que sempre transforma matrizes de densidade em matrizes de densidade, mesmo quando o canal é aplicado a apenas uma parte de um sistema composto.\n"
"O restante da lição é dedicado a uma prova matemática de que as três representações são equivalentes e capturam precisamente a definição.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Overview of the proof {#overview-of-the-proof}"
msgstr "Visão geral da prova {#overview-of-the-proof}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Our goal is to establish the equivalence of a collection of four statements, and we'll begin by writing them down precisely.\n"
"All four statements follow the same conventions that have been used throughout the lesson, namely that $\\Phi$ is a linear mapping from square matrices to square matrices, the rows and columns of the input matrices have been placed in correspondence with the classical states of a system $\\mathsf{X}$ (the input system), and the rows and columns of the output matrices have been placed in correspondence with the classical states of a system $\\mathsf{Y}$ (the output system).\n"
msgstr ""
"Nosso objetivo é estabelecer a equivalência de uma coleção de quatro afirmações, e começaremos escrevendo-as com precisão.\n"
"Todas as quatro afirmações seguem as mesmas convenções utilizadas ao longo da lição: $\\Phi$ é um mapeamento linear de matrizes quadradas para matrizes quadradas, as linhas e colunas das matrizes de entrada foram colocadas em correspondência com os estados clássicos de um sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ (o sistema de entrada), e as linhas e colunas das matrizes de saída foram colocadas em correspondência com os estados clássicos de um sistema $\\mathsf{Y}$ (o sistema de saída).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$\\Phi$ is a channel from $\\mathsf{X}$ to $\\mathsf{Y}.$ That is, $\\Phi$ "
"always transforms density matrices to density matrices, even when it acts on"
" one part of a larger compound system.\n"
msgstr ""
"$\\Phi$ é um canal de $\\mathsf{X}$ para $\\mathsf{Y}.$ Isto é, $\\Phi$ "
"sempre transforma matrizes de densidade em matrizes de densidade, mesmo "
"quando age sobre uma parte de um sistema composto maior.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The Choi matrix $J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite and satisfies the "
"condition $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"A matriz de Choi $J(\\Phi)$ é semidefinida positiva e satisfaz a condição "
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is a Kraus representation for $\\Phi.$ That is, there exist matrices "
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ for which the equation $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = "
"0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}$ is true for every input $\\rho,$ and that"
" satisfy the condition $\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Existe uma representação de Kraus para $\\Phi.$ Isto é, existem matrizes "
"$A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ para as quais a equação $\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = "
"0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}$ é verdadeira para toda entrada $\\rho,$ e"
" que satisfazem a condição $\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = "
"\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '4. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is a Stinespring representation for $\\Phi.$ That is, there exist "
"systems $\\mathsf{W}$ and $\\mathsf{G}$ for which the pairs "
"$(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ and $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ have the same "
"number of classical states, along with a unitary matrix $U$ representing a "
"unitary operation from $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ to "
"$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y}),$ such that $\\Phi(\\rho) = "
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}}\\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert"
" \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger} \\bigr).$\n"
msgstr ""
"Existe uma representação de Stinespring para $\\Phi.$ Isto é, existem "
"sistemas $\\mathsf{W}$ e $\\mathsf{G}$ para os quais os pares "
"$(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ e $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ têm o mesmo número"
" de estados clássicos, juntamente com uma matriz unitária $U$ representando "
"uma operação unitária de $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ para "
"$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y}),$ tal que $\\Phi(\\rho) = "
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}}\\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert"
" \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger} \\bigr).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way the proof works is that a cycle of implications is proved:\n"
"the first statement in our list implies the second, the second implies the third, the third implies the fourth, and the fourth statement implies the first.\n"
"This establishes that all four statements are equivalent — which is to say that they're either all true or all false for a given choice of $\\Phi$ — because the implications can be followed transitively from any one statement to any other.\n"
msgstr ""
"A forma como a prova funciona é que um ciclo de implicações é provado:\n"
"a primeira afirmação da nossa lista implica a segunda, a segunda implica a terceira, a terceira implica a quarta, e a quarta afirmação implica a primeira.\n"
"Isso estabelece que todas as quatro afirmações são equivalentes — ou seja, elas são todas verdadeiras ou todas falsas para uma dada escolha de $\\Phi$ — pois as implicações podem ser seguidas transitivamente de qualquer uma das afirmações para qualquer outra.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This is a common strategy when proving that a collection of statements are equivalent, and a useful trick to use in such a context is to set up the implications in a way that makes them as easy to prove as possible.\n"
"That is the case here — and in fact we've already encountered two of the four implications.\n"
msgstr ""
"Essa é uma estratégia comum ao provar que uma coleção de afirmações são equivalentes, e um truque útil a utilizar nesse contexto é configurar as implicações de forma a torná-las tão fáceis de provar quanto possível.\n"
"É o que acontece aqui — e na verdade já encontramos duas das quatro implicações.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Channels to Choi matrices {#channels-to-choi-matrices}"
msgstr "Canais para matrizes de Choi {#channels-to-choi-matrices}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Referring to the statements listed above by their numbers, the first implication to be proved is 1 $\\Rightarrow$ 2.\n"
"This implication was already discussed in the context of the Choi state of a channel.\n"
"Here we'll summarize the mathematical details.\n"
msgstr ""
"Referindo-nos às afirmações listadas acima por seus números, a primeira implicação a ser provada é 1 $\\Rightarrow$ 2.\n"
"Essa implicação já foi discutida no contexto do estado de Choi de um canal.\n"
"Aqui resumiremos os detalhes matemáticos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Assume that the classical state set of the input system $\\mathsf{X}$ is $\\Sigma$ and let $n = \\vert\\Sigma\\vert.$\n"
"Consider the situation in which $\\Phi$ is applied to the second of two copies of $\\mathsf{X}$ together in the state\n"
msgstr ""
"Suponha que o conjunto de estados clássicos do sistema de entrada $\\mathsf{X}$ seja $\\Sigma$ e seja $n = \\vert\\Sigma\\vert.$\n"
"Considere a situação em que $\\Phi$ é aplicado ao segundo de dois sistemas $\\mathsf{X}$ juntos no estado\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\sum_{a \\in \\Sigma} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle = \\frac{1}{\\sqrt{n}} \\sum_{a \\in \\Sigma} \\vert a \\rangle \\otimes \\vert a \\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "which, as a density matrix, is given by\n"
msgstr "que, como matriz de densidade, é dado por\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b \\in \\Sigma}\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert = \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b \\in \\Sigma}\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "The result can be written as\n"
msgstr "O resultado pode ser escrito como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"(\\operatorname{Id}\\otimes \\,\\Phi) \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\Phi\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{J(\\Phi)}{n},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"(\\operatorname{Id}\\otimes \\,\\Phi) \\bigl(\\vert \\psi \\rangle \\langle \\psi \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{1}{n} \\sum_{a,b = 0}^{n-1} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\Phi\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr)\n"
"= \\frac{J(\\Phi)}{n},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and by the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel this must be a density matrix.\n"
"Like all density matrices it must be positive semidefinite, and multiplying a positive semidefinite matrix by a positive real number yields another positive semidefinite matrix, and therefore $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0.$\n"
msgstr ""
"e pela suposição de que $\\Phi$ é um canal, isso deve ser uma matriz de densidade.\n"
"Como toda matriz de densidade, ela deve ser semidefinida positiva, e multiplicar uma matriz semidefinida positiva por um número real positivo resulta em outra matriz semidefinida positiva, portanto $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Moreover, under the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel, it must preserve "
"trace, and therefore\n"
msgstr ""
"Além disso, sob a suposição de que $\\Phi$ é um canal, ele deve preservar o "
"traço, e portanto\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\Phi( \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert)\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\Phi( \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert)\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\bigr) \\, \\vert a\\rangle\\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Choi to Kraus representations {#choi-to-kraus-representations}"
msgstr "Representações de Choi para Kraus {#choi-to-kraus-representations}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The second implication, again referring to the statements in our list by their numbers, is 2 $\\Rightarrow$ 3.\n"
"To be clear, we're ignoring the other statements — and in particular we cannot make the assumption that $\\Phi$ is a channel.\n"
"All we have to work with is that $\\Phi$ is a linear mapping whose Choi representation satisfies $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$ and\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"A segunda implicação, referindo-nos novamente às afirmações da nossa lista por seus números, é 2 $\\Rightarrow$ 3.\n"
"Para ser claro, estamos ignorando as demais afirmações — e em particular não podemos assumir que $\\Phi$ é um canal.\n"
"Tudo o que temos para trabalhar é que $\\Phi$ é um mapeamento linear cuja representação de Choi satisfaz $J(\\Phi) \\geq 0$ e\n"
"$\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This, however, is all we need to conclude that $\\Phi$ has a Kraus "
"representation\n"
msgstr ""
"Isso, no entanto, é suficiente para concluirmos que $\\Phi$ possui uma "
"representação de Kraus\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for which the condition\n"
msgstr "para a qual a condição\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "is satisfied.\n"
msgstr "é satisfeita.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We begin with the critically important assumption that $J(\\Phi)$ is "
"positive semidefinite, which means that it is possible to express it in the "
"form\n"
msgstr ""
"Começamos com a suposição criticamente importante de que $J(\\Phi)$ é "
"semidefinida positiva, o que significa que é possível expressá-la na forma\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert\n"
"\\tag{1}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for some way of choosing the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle.$\n"
"In general there will be multiple ways to do this — and in fact this directly mirrors the freedom one has in choosing a Kraus representation for $\\Phi.$\n"
msgstr ""
"para alguma escolha dos vetores $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle.$\n"
"Em geral haverá múltiplas formas de fazer isso — e de fato isso espelha diretamente a liberdade que se tem ao escolher uma representação de Kraus para $\\Phi.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"One way to obtain such an expression is to first use the spectral theorem to"
" write\n"
msgstr ""
"Uma forma de obter tal expressão é primeiro usar o teorema espectral para "
"escrever\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\gamma_k \\rangle \\langle \\gamma_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\lambda_k \\vert \\gamma_k \\rangle \\langle \\gamma_k \\vert,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"in which $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$ are the eigenvalues of "
"$J(\\Phi)$ (which are necessarily nonnegative real numbers because "
"$J(\\Phi)$ is positive semidefinite) and "
"$\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{N-1}\\rangle$ are unit "
"eigenvectors corresponding to the eigenvalues "
"$\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}.$\n"
msgstr ""
"em que $\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}$ são os autovalores de $J(\\Phi)$ "
"(que são necessariamente números reais não negativos pois $J(\\Phi)$ é "
"semidefinida positiva) e "
"$\\vert\\gamma_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\gamma_{N-1}\\rangle$ são "
"autovetores unitários correspondentes aos autovalores "
"$\\lambda_0,\\ldots,\\lambda_{N-1}.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Note that, while there's no freedom in choosing the eigenvalues (except for how they're ordered), there is freedom in the choice of the eigenvectors, particularly when there are eigenvalues with multiplicity larger than one.\n"
"So, this is not a unique expression of $J(\\Phi)$ — we're just assuming we have one such expression.\n"
"Regardless, because the eigenvalues are nonnegative real numbers, they have nonnegative square roots, and so we can select\n"
msgstr ""
"Observe que, embora não haja liberdade na escolha dos autovalores (exceto em como são ordenados), há liberdade na escolha dos autovetores, especialmente quando há autovalores com multiplicidade maior que um.\n"
"Portanto, essa não é uma expressão única de $J(\\Phi)$ — estamos apenas assumindo que temos uma tal expressão.\n"
"De qualquer forma, como os autovalores são números reais não negativos, eles têm raízes quadradas não negativas, e assim podemos selecionar\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\gamma_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sqrt{\\lambda_k} \\vert \\gamma_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for each $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$ to obtain an expression of the form $(1).$\n"
msgstr "para cada $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1$ para obter uma expressão na forma $(1).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It is, however, not essential that the expression $(1)$ comes from a spectral decomposition in this way, and in particular the vectors $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ need not be orthogonal in general.\n"
"It is noteworthy, though, that we can choose these vectors to be orthogonal if we wish — and moreover we never need $N$ to be larger than $nm$\n"
"(recalling that $n$ and $m$ denote the numbers of classical states of $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y},$ respectively).\n"
msgstr ""
"No entanto, não é essencial que a expressão $(1)$ venha de uma decomposição espectral dessa forma, e em particular os vetores $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ não precisam ser ortogonais em geral.\n"
"Vale notar, porém, que podemos escolher esses vetores para serem ortogonais se desejarmos — e além disso nunca precisamos que $N$ seja maior que $nm$\n"
"(lembrando que $n$ e $m$ denotam os números de estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y},$ respectivamente).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Next, each of the vectors "
"$\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ can be further "
"decomposed as\n"
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, cada um dos vetores "
"$\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ pode ser "
"decomposto como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle,\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where the vectors $\\{ \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle \\}$ have entries "
"corresponding to the classical states of $\\mathsf{Y}$ and can be explicitly"
" determined by the equation\n"
msgstr ""
"onde os vetores $\\{ \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle \\}$ possuem entradas "
"correspondentes aos estados clássicos de $\\mathsf{Y}$ e podem ser "
"determinados explicitamente pela equação\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle = \\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigr) \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle = \\bigl( \\langle a \\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{Y}}\\bigr) \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"for each $a\\in\\Sigma$ and $k=0,\\ldots,N-1.$\n"
"Although $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ are not necessarily unit vectors, this is the same process we would use to analyze what would happen if a standard basis measurement was performed on the system $\\mathsf{X}$ given a quantum state vector of the pair $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"
msgstr ""
"para cada $a\\in\\Sigma$ e $k=0,\\ldots,N-1.$\n"
"Embora $\\vert\\psi_0\\rangle,\\ldots,\\vert\\psi_{N-1}\\rangle$ não sejam necessariamente vetores unitários, esse é o mesmo processo que usaríamos para analisar o que aconteceria se uma medição na base padrão fosse realizada no sistema $\\mathsf{X}$ dado um vetor de estado quântico do par $(\\mathsf{X},\\mathsf{Y}).$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And now we come to the trick that makes this part of the proof work.\n"
"We define our Kraus matrices $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ according to the following equation.\n"
msgstr ""
"E agora chegamos ao truque que faz essa parte da prova funcionar.\n"
"Definimos nossas matrizes de Kraus $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ de acordo com a seguinte equação.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We can think about this formula purely symbolically: $\\vert a\\rangle$ effectively gets flipped around to form $\\langle a\\vert$ and moved to right-hand side, forming a matrix.\n"
"For the purposes of verifying the proof, the formula is all we need.\n"
msgstr ""
"Podemos pensar nessa fórmula de forma puramente simbólica: $\\vert a\\rangle$ é efetivamente invertido para formar $\\langle a\\vert$ e movido para o lado direito, formando uma matriz.\n"
"Para fins de verificação da prova, a fórmula é tudo o que precisamos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There is, however, a simple and intuitive relationship between the vector $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ and the matrix $A_k,$ which is that by *vectorizing* $A_k$ we get $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle.$\n"
"What it means to vectorize $A_k$ is that we stack the columns on top of one another (with the leftmost column on top proceeding to the rightmost on the bottom), in order to form a vector.\n"
"For instance, if $\\mathsf{X}$ and $\\mathsf{Y}$ are both qubits, and for some choice of $k$ we have\n"
msgstr ""
"Há, no entanto, uma relação simples e intuitiva entre o vetor $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle$ e a matriz $A_k,$ que é que ao *vetorizar* $A_k$ obtemos $\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle.$\n"
"Vetorizar $A_k$ significa empilhar as colunas umas sobre as outras (com a coluna mais à esquerda no topo, seguindo até a mais à direita na parte inferior), para formar um vetor.\n"
"Por exemplo, se $\\mathsf{X}$ e $\\mathsf{Y}$ são ambos qubits, e para alguma escolha de $k$ temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 0\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 0\\rangle +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle \\otimes \\vert 1\\rangle\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix},\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "then\n"
msgstr "então\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A_k & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{10}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"A_k & = \\alpha_{00} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{01} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{10} \\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert +\n"
"\\alpha_{11} \\vert 1\\rangle\\langle 1\\vert\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"\\alpha_{00} & \\alpha_{10}\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\alpha_{01} & \\alpha_{11}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(Beware: sometimes the vectorization of a matrix is defined in a slightly "
"different way, which is that the *rows* of the matrix are transposed and "
"stacked on top of one another to form a column vector.)\n"
msgstr ""
"(Atenção: às vezes a vetorização de uma matriz é definida de forma "
"ligeiramente diferente, em que as *linhas* da matriz são transpostas e "
"empilhadas umas sobre as outras para formar um vetor coluna.)\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"First we'll verify that this choice of Kraus matrices correctly describes the mapping $\\Phi,$ after which we'll verify the other required condition.\n"
"To keep things straight, let's define a new mapping $\\Psi$ as follows.\n"
msgstr ""
"Primeiro verificaremos que essa escolha de matrizes de Kraus descreve corretamente o mapeamento $\\Phi,$ após o que verificaremos a outra condição necessária.\n"
"Para manter as coisas claras, vamos definir um novo mapeamento $\\Psi$ da seguinte forma.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Psi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Psi(\\rho) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Thus, our goal is to verify that $\\Psi = \\Phi.$\n"
msgstr "Portanto, nosso objetivo é verificar que $\\Psi = \\Phi.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The way we can do this is to compare the Choi representations of these mappings.\n"
"Choi representations are faithful, so we have $\\Psi = \\Phi$ if and only if $J(\\Phi) = J(\\Psi).$\n"
"At this point we can simply compute $J(\\Psi)$ using the expressions\n"
msgstr ""
"A forma como podemos fazer isso é comparando as representações de Choi desses mapeamentos.\n"
"Representações de Choi são fiéis, então temos $\\Psi = \\Phi$ se e somente se $J(\\Phi) = J(\\Psi).$\n"
"Nesse ponto podemos simplesmente calcular $J(\\Psi)$ usando as expressões\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{and}\\quad\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert\\psi_k\\rangle = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\n"
"\\quad\\text{e}\\quad\n"
"A_k = \\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert \\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle a \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "together with the bilinearity of tensor products to simplify.\n"
msgstr ""
"juntamente com a bilinearidade dos produtos tensoriais para simplificar.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Psi) & = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert A_k^{\\dagger}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1}  \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle b\\vert \\otimes \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\\biggr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = J(\\Phi)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"J(\\Psi) & = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert A_k^{\\dagger}\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma}  \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1}  \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\biggl(\\sum_{a\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\otimes \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle\\biggr)\n"
"\\biggl(\\sum_{b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle b\\vert \\otimes \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\\biggr)\\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k \\rangle \\langle \\psi_k \\vert \\\\[2mm]\n"
"& = J(\\Phi)\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "So, our Kraus matrices correctly describe $\\Phi.$\n"
msgstr "Portanto, nossas matrizes de Kraus descrevem corretamente $\\Phi.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to check the required condition on $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1},$ which turns out to be equivalent to the assumption $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ (which we haven't used yet).\n"
"What we'll show is this relationship:\n"
msgstr ""
"Resta verificar a condição necessária sobre $A_0,\\ldots,A_{N-1},$ que acaba sendo equivalente à suposição $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}$ (que ainda não usamos).\n"
"O que mostraremos é esta relação:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr)^{T} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr)^{T} = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"\\tag{2}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"(in which we're referring the *matrix transpose* on the left-hand side).\n"
msgstr ""
"(em que estamos nos referindo à *transposta matricial* no lado esquerdo).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Starting on the left, we can first observe that\n"
msgstr "Começando pelo lado esquerdo, podemos primeiro observar que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T\n"
"& = \\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)^T\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T\n"
"& = \\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert b \\rangle \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\langle a \\vert\\Biggr)^T\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The last equality follows from the fact that the transpose is linear and "
"maps $\\vert b\\rangle\\langle a \\vert$ to $\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b "
"\\vert.$\n"
msgstr ""
"A última igualdade decorre do fato de que a transposta é linear e mapeia "
"$\\vert b\\rangle\\langle a \\vert$ em $\\vert a\\rangle\\langle b "
"\\vert.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Moving to the right-hand side of our equation, we have\n"
msgstr "Passando para o lado direito da nossa equação, temos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k \\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"J(\\Phi) = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert \\psi_k\\rangle\\langle\\psi_k \\vert\n"
"= \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert \\otimes \\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and therefore\n"
msgstr "e portanto\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\bigr)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}}(J(\\Phi))\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert\\phi_{k,a}\\rangle\\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\bigr)\\,\n"
"\\vert a\\rangle \\langle b \\vert\\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\sum_{a,b\\in\\Sigma} \\langle \\phi_{k,b} \\vert \\phi_{k,a} \\rangle \\vert a \\rangle  \\langle b \\vert.\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We've obtained the same result, and therefore the equation $(2)$ has been verified.\n"
"It follows, by the assumption $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},$ that\n"
msgstr ""
"Obtivemos o mesmo resultado, e portanto a equação $(2)$ foi verificada.\n"
"Segue-se, pela suposição $\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{Y}} (J(\\Phi)) = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}},$ que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Biggl(\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k\\Biggr)^T = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"and therefore, because the identity matrix is its own transpose, the "
"required condition is true.\n"
msgstr ""
"e portanto, como a matriz identidade é sua própria transposta, a condição "
"necessária é verdadeira.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Kraus to Stinespring representations {#kraus-to-stinespring-representations}"
msgstr ""
"Representação de Kraus para Stinespring {#kraus-to-stinespring-"
"representations}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Now suppose that we have a Kraus representation of a mapping\n"
msgstr "Suponha agora que temos uma representação de Kraus de um mapeamento\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for which\n"
msgstr "para o qual\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Our goal is to find a Stinespring representation for $\\Phi.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Nosso objetivo é encontrar uma representação de Stinespring para $\\Phi.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"What we'd like to do first is to choose the garbage system $\\mathsf{G}$ so that its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"For $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ and $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ to have the same size, however, it must be that\n"
"$n$ divides $m N,$ allowing us to take $\\mathsf{W}$ to have classical states $\\{0,\\ldots,d-1\\}$ for $d = mN/n.$\n"
msgstr ""
"O que gostaríamos de fazer primeiro é escolher o sistema de lixo $\\mathsf{G}$ de modo que seu conjunto de estados clássicos seja $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Para que $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ e $(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y})$ tenham o mesmo tamanho, porém, é necessário que\n"
"$n$ divida $m N,$ o que nos permite tomar $\\mathsf{W}$ com estados clássicos $\\{0,\\ldots,d-1\\}$ para $d = mN/n.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"For an arbitrary choice of $n,$ $m,$ and $N,$ it may not be the case that $mN/n$ is an integer, so we're not actually free to choose $\\mathsf{G}$ so that it's classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"But we can always increase $N$ arbitrarily in the Kraus representation by choosing $A_k = 0$ for however many additional values of $k$ that we wish.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para uma escolha arbitrária de $n,$ $m,$ e $N,$ pode não ser o caso de $mN/n$ ser um inteiro, portanto não somos de fato livres para escolher $\\mathsf{G}$ de modo que seu conjunto de estados clássicos seja $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Mas sempre podemos aumentar $N$ arbitrariamente na representação de Kraus escolhendo $A_k = 0$ para quantos valores adicionais de $k$ desejarmos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"So, if we tacitly assume that $mN/n$ is an integer, which is equivalent to $N$ being a multiple of $n/\\operatorname{gcd}(n,m),$ then we're free to take $\\mathsf{G}$ so that its classical state set is $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"In particular, if it is the case that $N = nm,$ then we may take $\\mathsf{W}$ to have $m^2$ classical states.\n"
msgstr ""
"Assim, se assumirmos tacitamente que $mN/n$ é um inteiro — o que equivale a $N$ ser múltiplo de $n/\\operatorname{gcd}(n,m)$ — então somos livres para tomar $\\mathsf{G}$ de modo que seu conjunto de estados clássicos seja $\\{0,\\ldots,N-1\\}.$\n"
"Em particular, se $N = nm,$ podemos tomar $\\mathsf{W}$ com $m^2$ estados clássicos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"It remains to choose $U,$ and we'll do this by matching the following "
"pattern.\n"
msgstr "Resta escolher $U,$ e faremos isso seguindo o padrão abaixo.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U =\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_{0} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1} & \\fbox{?} & \\cdots & \\fbox{?}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"To be clear, this pattern is meant to suggest a block matrix, where each block (including $A_{0},\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ as well as the blocks marked with a question mark) has $m$ rows and $n$ columns.\n"
"There are $N$ rows of blocks, which means that there are $d = mN/n$ columns of blocks.\n"
msgstr ""
"Para ficar claro, esse padrão pretende sugerir uma matriz em blocos, onde cada bloco (incluindo $A_{0},\\ldots,A_{N-1}$ bem como os blocos marcados com um ponto de interrogação) tem $m$ linhas e $n$ colunas.\n"
"Há $N$ linhas de blocos, o que significa que há $d = mN/n$ colunas de blocos.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Expressed in more formulaic terms, we will define $U$ as\n"
msgstr "Expresso em termos mais formais, definiremos $U$ como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U & = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\sum_{j=0}^{d-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle j \\vert \\otimes M_{k,j} \\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} & \\cdots & M_{0,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1} & \\cdots & M_{1,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{N-1,0} & M_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & M_{N-1,d-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"U & = \\sum_{k=0}^{N-1} \\sum_{j=0}^{d-1} \\vert k \\rangle \\langle j \\vert \\otimes M_{k,j} \\\\[4mm]\n"
"& = \\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"M_{0,0} & M_{0,1} & \\cdots & M_{0,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{1,0} & M_{1,1} & \\cdots & M_{1,d-1} \\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots & \\vdots & \\ddots & \\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"M_{N-1,0} & M_{N-1,1} & \\cdots & M_{N-1,d-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"where each matrix $M_{k,j}$ has $m$ rows and $n$ columns, and in particular "
"we shall take $M_{k,0} = A_k$ for $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1.$\n"
msgstr ""
"onde cada matriz $M_{k,j}$ tem $m$ linhas e $n$ colunas, e em particular "
"tomaremos $M_{k,0} = A_k$ para $k = 0,\\ldots,N-1.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This must be a unitary matrix, and the blocks labeled with a question mark, "
"or equivalently $M_{k,j}$ for $j>0,$ must be selected with this in mind — "
"but aside from allowing $U$ to be unitary, the blocks labeled with a "
"question mark won't have any relevance to the proof.\n"
msgstr ""
"Essa deve ser uma matriz unitária, e os blocos marcados com ponto de "
"interrogação — ou equivalentemente $M_{k,j}$ para $j>0$ — devem ser "
"escolhidos com isso em mente; mas além de permitir que $U$ seja unitária, "
"esses blocos não terão nenhuma relevância para a prova.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Let's momentarily disregard the concern that $U$ is unitary and focus on the"
" expression\n"
msgstr ""
"Vamos momentaneamente ignorar a preocupação de que $U$ seja unitária e nos "
"concentrar na expressão\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"that describes the output state of $\\mathsf{Y}$ given the input state $\\rho$ of $\\mathsf{X}$ for our Stinespring representation.\n"
"We can alternatively write\n"
msgstr ""
"que descreve o estado de saída de $\\mathsf{Y}$ dado o estado de entrada $\\rho$ de $\\mathsf{X}$ para nossa representação de Stinespring.\n"
"Podemos escrever alternativamente\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) \\rho (\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) U^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) \\rho (\\langle 0\\vert \\otimes \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) U^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and we see from our choice of $U$ that\n"
msgstr "e vemos pela nossa escolha de $U$ que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\otimes\\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}) =\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "We therefore find that\n"
msgstr "Portanto, concluímos que\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert \\otimes A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"U(\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0 \\vert \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\n"
"= \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert \\otimes A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger},\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "and so\n"
msgstr "e assim\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"& = \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert\\bigr) \\, A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\Phi(\\rho).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{aligned}\n"
"\\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho) U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"& = \\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\operatorname{Tr}\\bigl(\\vert k\\rangle\\langle j\\vert\\bigr) \\, A_k \\rho A_j^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k \\rho A_k^{\\dagger} \\\\\n"
"& = \\Phi(\\rho).\n"
"\\end{aligned}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We therefore have a correct representation for the mapping $\\Phi,$ and it "
"remains to verify that we can choose $U$ to be unitary.\n"
msgstr ""
"Temos, portanto, uma representação correta para o mapeamento $\\Phi,$ e "
"resta verificar que podemos escolher $U$ como unitária.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Consider the first $n$ columns of $U$ when it's selected according to the pattern above.\n"
"Taking these columns alone, we have a block matrix\n"
msgstr ""
"Considere as primeiras $n$ colunas de $U$ quando ela é escolhida de acordo com o padrão acima.\n"
"Tomando apenas essas colunas, temos uma matriz em blocos\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\begin{pmatrix}\n"
"A_0\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_1\\\\[1mm]\n"
"\\vdots\\\\[1mm]\n"
"A_{N-1}\n"
"\\end{pmatrix}.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"There are $n$ columns, one for each classical state of $\\mathsf{X},$ and as vectors let us name the columns as $\\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle$ for each $a\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
"Here's a formula for these vectors that can be matched to the block matrix representation above.\n"
msgstr ""
"Há $n$ colunas, uma para cada estado clássico de $\\mathsf{X},$ e como vetores vamos nomear as colunas como $\\vert \\gamma_a \\rangle$ para cada $a\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
"Aqui está uma fórmula para esses vetores que pode ser relacionada à representação em blocos acima.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\gamma_a\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert \\gamma_a\\rangle = \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} \\vert k\\rangle \\otimes A_k \\vert a \\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Now let's compute the inner product between any two of these vectors, "
"meaning the ones corresponding to any choice of $a,b\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
msgstr ""
"Agora vamos calcular o produto interno entre quaisquer dois desses vetores, "
"ou seja, os correspondentes a qualquer escolha de $a,b\\in\\Sigma.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle k \\vert j \\rangle \\, \\langle a \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} A_j \\vert b\\rangle =\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr) \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle =\n"
"\\sum_{j,k = 0}^{N-1} \\langle k \\vert j \\rangle \\, \\langle a \\vert A_k^{\\dagger} A_j \\vert b\\rangle =\n"
"\\langle a \\vert \\Biggl( \\sum_{k = 0}^{N-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k \\Biggr) \\vert b\\rangle\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "By the assumption\n"
msgstr "Pela hipótese\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\sum_{k = 0}^{m-1} A_k^{\\dagger} A_k = \\mathbb{I}_{\\mathsf{X}}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"we conclude that the $n$ column vectors "
"$\\{\\vert\\gamma_a\\rangle\\,:\\,a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ form an orthonormal "
"set:\n"
msgstr ""
"concluímos que os $n$ vetores coluna "
"$\\{\\vert\\gamma_a\\rangle\\,:\\,a\\in\\Sigma\\}$ formam um conjunto "
"ortonormal:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & a = b\\\\\n"
"0 & a\\neq b\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\langle \\gamma_a \\vert \\gamma_b \\rangle = \\begin{cases}\n"
"1 & a = b\\\\\n"
"0 & a\\neq b\n"
"\\end{cases}\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "for all $a,b\\in\\Sigma.$\n"
msgstr "para todo $a,b\\in\\Sigma.$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This implies that it is possible to fill out the remaining columns of $U$ so that it becomes a unitary matrix.\n"
"In particular, the Gram-Schmidt orthogonalization process can be used to select the remaining columns.\n"
"Something similar was done in the *Quantum circuits* lesson of \"Basics of quantum information\" in the context of the state discrimination problem.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isso implica que é possível completar as colunas restantes de $U$ de modo que ela se torne uma matriz unitária.\n"
"Em particular, o processo de ortonormalização de Gram-Schmidt pode ser usado para selecionar as colunas restantes.\n"
"Algo semelhante foi feito na lição *Circuitos quânticos* de \"Fundamentos de informação quântica\" no contexto do problema de discriminação de estados.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Title ##
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Stinespring representations back to the definition {#stinespring-"
"representations-back-to-the-definition}"
msgstr ""
"Representações de Stinespring de volta à definição {#stinespring-"
"representations-back-to-the-definition}"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"The final implication is 4 $\\Rightarrow$ 1.\n"
"That is, we assume that we have a unitary operation transforming a pair of systems $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ into a pair\n"
"$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y}),$ and our goal is to conclude that the mapping\n"
msgstr ""
"A implicação final é 4 $\\Rightarrow$ 1.\n"
"Ou seja, assumimos que temos uma operação unitária transformando um par de sistemas $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{X})$ em um par\n"
"$(\\mathsf{G},\\mathsf{Y}),$ e nosso objetivo é concluir que o mapeamento\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\Phi(\\rho) = \\operatorname{Tr}_{\\mathsf{G}} \\bigl( U (\\vert 0\\rangle \\langle 0 \\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\rho)U^{\\dagger}\\bigr)\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"is a valid channel.\n"
"From its form, it is evident that $\\Phi$ is linear, and it remains to verify that it always transforms density matrices into density matrices.\n"
"This is pretty straightforward and we've already discussed the key points.\n"
msgstr ""
"é um canal válido.\n"
"Pela sua forma, fica evidente que $\\Phi$ é linear, e resta verificar que ela sempre transforma matrizes densidade em matrizes densidade.\n"
"Isso é bastante direto e já discutimos os pontos principais.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"In particular, if we start with a density matrix $\\sigma$ of a compound system $(\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X}),$ and then add on an additional workspace system $\\mathsf{W},$ we will certainly be left with a density matrix.\n"
"If we reorder the systems $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$ for convenience, we can write this state as\n"
msgstr ""
"Em particular, se começarmos com uma matriz densidade $\\sigma$ de um sistema composto $(\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X}),$ e em seguida adicionarmos um sistema de espaço de trabalho $\\mathsf{W},$ certamente continuaremos com uma matriz densidade.\n"
"Se reordenarmos os sistemas $(\\mathsf{W},\\mathsf{Z},\\mathsf{X})$ por conveniência, podemos escrever esse estado como\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\sigma.\n"
"$$\n"
msgstr ""
"$$\n"
"\\vert 0\\rangle\\langle 0\\vert_{\\mathsf{W}} \\otimes \\sigma.\n"
"$$\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"We then apply the unitary operation $U,$ and as we already discussed this is a valid channel, and hence maps density matrices to density matrices.\n"
"Finally, the partial trace of a density matrix is another density matrix.\n"
msgstr ""
"Em seguida, aplicamos a operação unitária $U,$ e como já discutimos, isso é um canal válido e, portanto, mapeia matrizes densidade em matrizes densidade.\n"
"Por fim, o traço parcial de uma matriz densidade é outra matriz densidade.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"Another way to say this is to observe first that each of these things is a "
"valid channel:\n"
msgstr ""
"Outra maneira de dizer isso é observar primeiro que cada uma dessas coisas é"
" um canal válido:\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '1. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Introducing an initialized workspace system.\n"
msgstr "Introduzir um sistema de espaço de trabalho inicializado.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '2. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Performing a unitary operation.\n"
msgstr "Realizar uma operação unitária.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Bullet: '3. '
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid "Tracing out a system.\n"
msgstr "Traçar um sistema (traço parcial).\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"And finally, any composition of channels is another channel — which is "
"immediate from the definition, but is also a fact worth observing in its own"
" right.\n"
msgstr ""
"E por fim, qualquer composição de canais é outro canal — o que é imediato a "
"partir da definição, mas também é um fato que vale a pena observar por si "
"só.\n"

# doq-bootstrap: positional
#. type: Plain text
#, markdown-text, no-wrap
msgid ""
"This completes the proof of the final implication, and therefore we've "
"established the equivalence of the four statements listed at the start of "
"the section.\n"
msgstr ""
"Isso completa a prova da implicação final e, portanto, estabelecemos a "
"equivalência das quatro afirmações listadas no início da seção.\n"
